Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/25] Modeling Algorithms - Use the builder angular tolerance
 to count sharp edges at a corner

At the end of a fillet, ChFi3d_NumberOfSharpEdges() decides how the corner
is built (OneCorner for up to three sharp edges, IntersectionAtEnd for
more). It treated an edge as smooth when ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces() found
its faces within the fixed G1 tolerance of LocalAnalysis_SurfaceContinuity,
0.1 rad (5.7 degrees). A real kink of a few degrees was therefore ignored.

Example (FreeCAD issue 29234): a tapered shaft starting flush with the
faces of a plate. At the root of the shaft the tapered faces meet the plate
faces at 1.4 degrees, so the end vertex of each long shaft edge has four
sharp edges but was treated as a corner of three. The OnSame corner then
either failed (faulty vertex) or produced a self-intersecting wire on the
tapered face.

ChFi3d::IsTangentFaces() gets an optional angular tolerance (default
unchanged), and the sharp edge count at a vertex uses the angular
tolerance of the builder (1.e-2 by default, set by SetParams()). Other
callers of IsTangentFaces() are not changed.

